course: dictionary
lesson: 3745
title: A pot for growing plants
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A flowerpot is a container for growing a plant in. You can see the word is made of two smaller words, flower and pot, and a pot is a good clue for what it holds. «Woodlice hide under flowerpots» tells you that flowerpots are things you can find outside, where woodlice can crawl beneath them.
explain: Most flowerpots have a hole in the bottom. The hole lets extra water drain out so the roots do not sit in water. If you read about a flowerpot in a science text, look for this hole, because it is part of what the word means.
explain: The word can also be a name. «Bill and Ben, the Flowerpot Men» were puppets in an old children's programme on UK TV. A capital letter and the words around it, like the names Bill and Ben, tell you this is a name and not an ordinary pot.
fact: A flowerpot is a container for growing a plant in.
fact: Flowerpots are usually made of clay or plastic.
fact: Most flowerpots have a hole in the bottom so that extra water can drain out.
fact: «Woodlice hide under flowerpots» shows that flowerpots can be found in gardens and outdoor places.
fact: «Bill and Ben, the Flowerpot Men» were puppets in an old children's programme. Here Flowerpot is a name, so it has a capital letter.
exercise: What is a flowerpot? | A kind of small wild animal | *A container for growing a plant in | A tool for digging holes | A bag for carrying soil
exercise: Most flowerpots have a hole in the bottom. What is the hole for? | *Letting extra water drain out | Letting light shine in | Letting air out for the plant | Letting soil fall out on purpose
exercise: Bill and Ben, the Flowerpot Men, were what? | Real gardeners on TV | *Puppets in an old children's programme | Plants with names | Two clay pots for plants
test: What are flowerpots usually made of? | Wood or tin | Glass or paper | Wool or sand | *Clay or plastic
test: In a science test, why do pupils use identical flowerpots? | To make the test shorter | To make the plants grow faster | *To keep the test fair | To make the pots look nice
exam: «Woodlice hide under flowerpots.» Find and copy the word that means a container for growing a plant. | spiders | *flowerpots | woodlice | hide
